# Representing a nested collection
#
# A list holds a number, a blank node and a nested list, and is the subject of
# a statement. The example shows that such a collection is read correctly;
# its only output is a short Markdown note listing the example's files.

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyeron/examples/collection#> .

# A list as the subject of a statement. Its second member is the blank node
# _:b2, which the next statement describes; its third member is a list.
(1 _:b2 (2)) :p2 :q2 .
_:b2 :p :q .

# Markdown rendering via log:outputString.
:__md_output :text "# collection\n\n## Source files\n\n- [N3 rules](../collection.n3)\n- [Input TriG](../input/collection.trig)\n\n" .
{
    :__md_output :text ?text
} log:query {
    :__md_output log:outputString ?text
} .
